      "hints": [
        "Use binomial formula: $1 + \\binom{5}{1}(-2x) + \\binom{5}{2}(-2x)^2$.",
        "Evaluate: $1 - 10x + 40x^2$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Apply the binomial expansion formula for $(1 - 2x)^5$ up to the term in $x^2$:\n$$(1 - 2x)^5 = 1 + \\binom{5}{1}(-2x) + \\binom{5}{2}(-2x)^2 + \\dots$$",
        "Simplify each term:\n$$1 + 5(-2x) + 10(4x^2) = 1 - 10x + 40x^2$$"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_id": "9709_s18_11_q1_ii",
      "difficulty": 2,
      "mapping": {
        "topic_id": "9709_p1_t_series",
        "lesson_id": "9709_p1_t_series_m01_l02"
      },
      "hints": [
        "Collect terms: $1(40) + a(-10) + 2(1) = 42 - 10a$.",
        "Set $42 - 10a = 12 \\implies 10a = 30 \\implies a = 3$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Multiply the relevant terms from $(1 + ax + 2x^2)(1 - 10x + 40x^2 + \\dots)$ that yield $x^2$:\n$$\\text{Term in } x^2 = 1(40x^2) + ax(-10x) + 2x^2(1)$$",
        "Combine the coefficients:\n$$(40 - 10a + 2)x^2 = (42 - 10a)x^2$$",
        "Equate the coefficient to 12 and solve for $a$:\n$$42 - 10a = 12 \\implies 10a = 30 \\implies a = 3$$"
      ]
    }
  ]
